A.mc("e2-c9-standard-10-check","c9-10-core","What links cyanobacteria with the source’s banded iron formation?",["*They supplied oxygen that promoted oxidation and iron precipitation|Photosynthetic oxygen changed dissolved-iron chemistry and favored iron-rich precipitation.", "They released dissolved iron that replaced oxygen in surface waters|The stated role of cyanobacteria is oxygen production, rather than supplying the dissolved iron.", "They formed hard skeletons that accumulated as iron-rich limestone|The source describes mainly iron oxides and quartz, rather than a limestone made of animal skeletons.", "They consumed oxygen so iron stayed oxidized and dissolved in seawater|This reverses the described oxygen-production and iron-precipitation relationship."],"Photosynthetic oxygen changed dissolved-iron chemistry and favored iron-rich precipitation.",["TB9:9.10"],{"examId": "exam2", "mock": false, "topics": ["E2C9S10"], "media": {"kind": "img", "src": "animations/chapter9/source/9.10-p3-Im1.png", "alt": "Original course illustration for section 9.10, PDF page 3", "cap": "Exploring Geology · 9.10 · PDF p3 · unchanged original figure"}, "sourceFigure": true});
