A.mc("e2-c9-standard-12-check","c9-12-core","Mammals occur in Mesozoic reconstructions. What does age of mammals mean for the Cenozoic?",["*Mammals became especially diverse and prominent during that era|Mammals existed earlier and diversified prominently during the Cenozoic.", "Mammals first evolved after the end-Cretaceous extinction|The supplied Mesozoic evidence already includes mammals.", "The era began with the first appearance of vertebrate animals|Vertebrates appeared earlier; Cenozoic mammal prominence is a different event.", "The era began with the earliest colonization of land by animals|Land colonization occurred earlier and does not define the Cenozoic age-of-mammals label."],"Mammals existed earlier and diversified prominently during the Cenozoic.",["TB9:9.12"],{"examId": "exam2", "mock": false, "topics": ["E2C9S12"], "media": {"kind": "img", "src": "animations/chapter9/source/9.12-p5-Im2.png", "alt": "Original course illustration for section 9.12, PDF page 5", "cap": "Exploring Geology · 9.12 · PDF p5 · unchanged original figure"}, "sourceFigure": true});
