A.mc("e2-c9-standard-13-check","c9-13-core","Same-age coastal beds formed in a sandy nearshore setting and a muddy offshore setting. What should correlation allow?",["*Different rock types within a shared time interval|Lateral depositional environments can produce different facies at the same time.", "Identical lithology wherever beds have the same age|Equal age does not require identical sediment or lithology across changing environments.", "Matching thickness instead of comparing age evidence|Thickness varies with accumulation and preservation and cannot replace age evidence.", "Treating the sandy bed as older because it is nearer shore|Position within a contemporaneous environment does not by itself make that bed older."],"Lateral depositional environments can produce different facies at the same time.",["TB9:9.13"],{"examId": "exam2", "mock": false, "topics": ["E2C9S13"], "media": {"kind": "img", "src": "animations/chapter9/source/9.13-p5-Im1.png", "alt": "Original course illustration for section 9.13, PDF page 5", "cap": "Exploring Geology · 9.13 · PDF p5 · unchanged original figure"}, "sourceFigure": true});
